  "stage6Description": "To remove the 1/|r| blur, projections are filtered before backprojection (Filtered Backprojection, FBP). Convolving each projection with Frank Natterer’s discrete ramp filter kernel w_b(l) = b² / (π⁴(1 - 4l²)) acts like an edge-sharpening derivative filter that adds negative side lobes. When backprojected, these negative lobes cancel the smearing exactly, yielding precise interior attenuation: ≈ 1.0 inside the phantom disk and ≈ 0.0 outside.",
  "@stage6Description": {
    "description": "Full description text for Stage 6 in wide layout"
  },
  "stage6Instruction1": "Step 1 of 2: Click inside the phantom disk. Observe the sharp edge lobes in the 1D profile and the reconstructed integral ≈ 1.0.",
  "@stage6Instruction1": {
    "description": "Step 1 interaction prompt for Stage 6 in wide layout"
  },
  "stage6Instruction2": "Step 2 of 2: Click outside the phantom disk. Notice how the negative side lobes cancel the smearing, yielding integral ≈ 0.0.",
  "@stage6Instruction2": {
    "description": "Step 2 interaction prompt for Stage 6 in wide layout"
  },
  "stage6NarrowDescription": "High-pass filtering the projections with Frank Natterer’s discrete filter kernel w_b(l) = b² / (π⁴(1 - 4l²)) sharpens the sinogram. Backprojecting the filtered data reconstructs the exact interior attenuation values: ≈ 1.0 inside the phantom and ≈ 0.0 outside.",
  "@stage6NarrowDescription": {
    "description": "Concise description text for Stage 6 in narrow layout"
  },
  "stage6NarrowInstruction1": "Step 1 of 2: Click inside the phantom disk. Observe the sharp edge lobes in the 1D profile and integral ≈ 1.0.",
  "@stage6NarrowInstruction1": {
    "description": "Step 1 interaction prompt for Stage 6 in narrow layout"
  },
  "stage6NarrowInstruction2": "Step 2 of 2: Click outside the phantom disk. Negative side lobes cancel smearing, yielding integral ≈ 0.0.",
  "@stage6NarrowInstruction2": {
    "description": "Step 2 interaction prompt for Stage 6 in narrow layout"
  },
  "stage6NarrowSubtitle": "Filtered Backprojection (FBP)",
